          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On November 5, 1976, at 5:00 PM and 8:08 PM, individuals observed the passage of a bright white light in the sky. This phenomenon, of circular shape, moved quickly along a northeast trajectory. No noise was heard during the observation, which lasted for a few seconds. Too few details were provided to validate a specific hypothesis. This case is classified as C due to a lack of information.",
